# The VM shell for design.md §D6.2's divergence probe.
#
#   gene run divergence
#
# All it does is print. The probe itself is `probes/divergence.gene`, which is a
# `^profile web` module and therefore runs unchanged on both backends — this
# file exists because stdout does not: `$println` is a VM builtin, and the web
# profile has no equivalent because a browser has nowhere to print to. Keeping
# it here rather than behind a conditional inside the probe is the same rule
# design.md §D3 applies to the whole system: platform edges live in shells.

(mod run_divergence)

(import [report] from "./divergence.gene")

(fn main [args] : Nil
  ($println (report)))
